  user_input {
    user_response: "L\303\240m l\341\272\241i v\341\273\233i prompt m\341\273\233i nh\306\260 sau\n# PROMPT \342\200\224 RECREATE LANDING PAGE FROM PROVIDED CSS, SVG & IMAGES\n\n## 1. ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n\nAct as a Senior Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, and Design System Engineer.\n\nYour task is to build a complete, responsive, production-quality landing page based strictly on the CSS files, SVG assets, images, and other reference materials I provide.\n\n**The primary objective is DESIGN FIDELITY, not creative redesign.**\n\nReconstruct the original visual system as accurately as possible while preserving the existing structure, design language, layout, and graphical assets.\n\n## 2. STRICT DESIGN PRESERVATION\n\nYou MUST preserve the following elements from the provided references:\n\n- Original CSS styling, including colors, gradients, shadows, borders, and effects.\n- Original SVG assets, vector illustrations, shapes, and icons.\n- Original images, including their proportions, crop behavior, and placement.\n- Original typography, including font families, sizes, weights, line heights, and letter spacing.\n- Original spacing system, margins, padding, alignment, and section proportions.\n- Original visual hierarchy and content structure.\n- Original navigation layout, buttons, cards, backgrounds, and section order.\n- Original animations, hover effects, transitions, and visual interactions where provided.\n\n**DO NOT:**\n- Redesign or reinterpret the original interface.\n- Replace supplied SVGs with alternative icons.\n- Generate substitute images when originals are available.\n- Introduce unrelated components or sections.\n- Change the original color palette or design theme.\n- Simplify complex layouts without technical necessity.\n- Apply generic landing page templates.\n- Add decorative elements not present in the references.\n\n## 3. TEXT REPLACEMENT RULES\n\nPreserve the original content structure and placement, but replace the visible textual content with placeholders.\n\nFollow these rules:\n\n**Headings**\n- Replace main headings with \"Title\".\n- Replace section headings with \"Section Title\".\n- Replace smaller headings with \"Subtitle\".\n\n**Paragraphs**\n- Replace paragraph content with Lorem Ipsum.\n- Match the approximate character length and line count of the original text.\n- Preserve the approximate original text density to maintain layout consistency.\n\n**Other text**\n- Navigation labels may use short generic placeholders.\n- Button labels may use \"Learn More\", \"Get Started\", or \"Explore\".\n- Form placeholders may use generic descriptive labels.\n\n**Important:** Do not change the number, order, or visual position of text blocks. Text replacement must not significantly alter the original layout.\n\n## 4. CSS & SVG HANDLING\n\nTreat the provided CSS and SVG files as authoritative design references.\n\n- Reuse original CSS classes and styles whenever technically feasible.\n- Preserve SVG `viewBox`, paths, fills, strokes, gradients, and proportions.\n- Avoid modifying SVG geometry.\n- Maintain image aspect ratios.\n- Do not rasterize SVG files unnecessarily.\n- Prioritize original assets over third-party libraries.\n- Use existing fonts and visual tokens when supplied.\n\nIf there are conflicts between generic framework defaults and the provided CSS, **the provided CSS takes priority**.\n\n## 5. LANDING PAGE IMPLEMENTATION\n\nBuild the complete landing page using the supplied references.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Semantic and maintainable code.\n- Responsive layouts for desktop, tablet, and mobile.\n- Accurate section composition.\n- Consistent spacing and typography.\n- Functional navigation and buttons where applicable.\n- Appropriate hover and focus states.\n- Smooth rendering and stable layouts.\n- Reusable components without changing their original visual appearance.\n\nDo not introduce new features merely to make the website more elaborate.\n\n## 6. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nPreserve the desktop design as the primary visual reference.\n\nFor smaller screens:\n\n- Adapt the layout without changing the design identity.\n- Preserve the original hierarchy.\n- Maintain readable typography.\n- Scale SVGs and images proportionally.\n- Avoid horizontal overflow.\n- Ensure appropriate touch targets.\n- Preserve the intended appearance of cards, buttons, and sections.\n\nDo not invent an entirely different mobile design.\n\n## 7. ASSET PRIORITY\n\nUse the following priority order:\n\n1. Provided CSS files.\n2. Provided SVG assets.\n3. Provided original images.\n4. Provided screenshots and visual references.\n5. Minimal technical adjustments required for responsiveness.\n\nDo not substitute existing assets with generated alternatives.\n\nIf an asset is unavailable, explicitly identify what is missing rather than silently inventing a replacement.\n\n## 8. IMPLEMENTATION WORKFLOW\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n1. Analyze all provided reference materials.\n2. Identify the original page structure.\n3. Extract the design system from the CSS.\n4. Map SVG and image assets to their appropriate sections.\n5. Identify typography, spacing, colors, and reusable components.\n6. Reconstruct the landing page.\n7. Replace only text content according to the placeholder rules.\n8. Verify visual fidelity and responsive behavior.\n\n## 9. FINAL QUALITY CHECK\n\nBefore completing the landing page, verify:\n\n- All available original assets are reused correctly.\n- Sections follow the original reference.\n- Colors, borders, shadows, spacing, and typography match the supplied design.\n- Text is replaced with the required placeholders.\n- No unauthorized elements have been introduced.\n- SVG geometry and image proportions are preserved.\n- Desktop and mobile layouts function correctly.\n\n## 10. ABSOLUTE RULE\n\n**PRESERVE THE ORIGINAL DESIGN. REPLACE ONLY THE TEXT.**\n\nThe finished landing page should visually resemble the supplied references as closely as possible, with only placeholder headings and Lorem Ipsum body text replacing the original written content.\n\nDo not redesign. Do not reinterpret. Do not add unnecessary creativity.\n\n**Design fidelity takes precedence over visual novelty.**"
    items {
      text: "L\303\240m l\341\272\241i v\341\273\233i prompt m\341\273\233i nh\306\260 sau\n# PROMPT \342\200\224 RECREATE LANDING PAGE FROM PROVIDED CSS, SVG & IMAGES\n\n## 1. ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n\nAct as a Senior Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, and Design System Engineer.\n\nYour task is to build a complete, responsive, production-quality landing page based strictly on the CSS files, SVG assets, images, and other reference materials I provide.\n\n**The primary objective is DESIGN FIDELITY, not creative redesign.**\n\nReconstruct the original visual system as accurately as possible while preserving the existing structure, design language, layout, and graphical assets.\n\n## 2. STRICT DESIGN PRESERVATION\n\nYou MUST preserve the following elements from the provided references:\n\n- Original CSS styling, including colors, gradients, shadows, borders, and effects.\n- Original SVG assets, vector illustrations, shapes, and icons.\n- Original images, including their proportions, crop behavior, and placement.\n- Original typography, including font families, sizes, weights, line heights, and letter spacing.\n- Original spacing system, margins, padding, alignment, and section proportions.\n- Original visual hierarchy and content structure.\n- Original navigation layout, buttons, cards, backgrounds, and section order.\n- Original animations, hover effects, transitions, and visual interactions where provided.\n\n**DO NOT:**\n- Redesign or reinterpret the original interface.\n- Replace supplied SVGs with alternative icons.\n- Generate substitute images when originals are available.\n- Introduce unrelated components or sections.\n- Change the original color palette or design theme.\n- Simplify complex layouts without technical necessity.\n- Apply generic landing page templates.\n- Add decorative elements not present in the references.\n\n## 3. TEXT REPLACEMENT RULES\n\nPreserve the original content structure and placement, but replace the visible textual content with placeholders.\n\nFollow these rules:\n\n**Headings**\n- Replace main headings with \"Title\".\n- Replace section headings with \"Section Title\".\n- Replace smaller headings with \"Subtitle\".\n\n**Paragraphs**\n- Replace paragraph content with Lorem Ipsum.\n- Match the approximate character length and line count of the original text.\n- Preserve the approximate original text density to maintain layout consistency.\n\n**Other text**\n- Navigation labels may use short generic placeholders.\n- Button labels may use \"Learn More\", \"Get Started\", or \"Explore\".\n- Form placeholders may use generic descriptive labels.\n\n**Important:** Do not change the number, order, or visual position of text blocks. Text replacement must not significantly alter the original layout.\n\n## 4. CSS & SVG HANDLING\n\nTreat the provided CSS and SVG files as authoritative design references.\n\n- Reuse original CSS classes and styles whenever technically feasible.\n- Preserve SVG `viewBox`, paths, fills, strokes, gradients, and proportions.\n- Avoid modifying SVG geometry.\n- Maintain image aspect ratios.\n- Do not rasterize SVG files unnecessarily.\n- Prioritize original assets over third-party libraries.\n- Use existing fonts and visual tokens when supplied.\n\nIf there are conflicts between generic framework defaults and the provided CSS, **the provided CSS takes priority**.\n\n## 5. LANDING PAGE IMPLEMENTATION\n\nBuild the complete landing page using the supplied references.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Semantic and maintainable code.\n- Responsive layouts for desktop, tablet, and mobile.\n- Accurate section composition.\n- Consistent spacing and typography.\n- Functional navigation and buttons where applicable.\n- Appropriate hover and focus states.\n- Smooth rendering and stable layouts.\n- Reusable components without changing their original visual appearance.\n\nDo not introduce new features merely to make the website more elaborate.\n\n## 6. RESPONSIVE DESIGN\n\nPreserve the desktop design as the primary visual reference.\n\nFor smaller screens:\n\n- Adapt the layout without changing the design identity.\n- Preserve the original hierarchy.\n- Maintain readable typography.\n- Scale SVGs and images proportionally.\n- Avoid horizontal overflow.\n- Ensure appropriate touch targets.\n- Preserve the intended appearance of cards, buttons, and sections.\n\nDo not invent an entirely different mobile design.\n\n## 7. ASSET PRIORITY\n\nUse the following priority order:\n\n1. Provided CSS files.\n2. Provided SVG assets.\n3. Provided original images.\n4. Provided screenshots and visual references.\n5. Minimal technical adjustments required for responsiveness.\n\nDo not substitute existing assets with generated alternatives.\n\nIf an asset is unavailable, explicitly identify what is missing rather than silently inventing a replacement.\n\n## 8. IMPLEMENTATION WORKFLOW\n\nBefore implementing:\n\n1. Analyze all provided reference materials.\n2. Identify the original page structure.\n3. Extract the design system from the CSS.\n4. Map SVG and image assets to their appropriate sections.\n5. Identify typography, spacing, colors, and reusable components.\n6. Reconstruct the landing page.\n7. Replace only text content according to the placeholder rules.\n8. Verify visual fidelity and responsive behavior.\n\n## 9. FINAL QUALITY CHECK\n\nBefore completing the landing page, verify:\n\n- All available original assets are reused correctly.\n- Sections follow the original reference.\n- Colors, borders, shadows, spacing, and typography match the supplied design.\n- Text is replaced with the required placeholders.\n- No unauthorized elements have been introduced.\n- SVG geometry and image proportions are preserved.\n- Desktop and mobile layouts function correctly.\n\n## 10. ABSOLUTE RULE\n\n**PRESERVE THE ORIGINAL DESIGN. REPLACE ONLY THE TEXT.**\n\nThe finished landing page should visually resemble the supplied references as closely as possible, with only placeholder headings and Lorem Ipsum body text replacing the original written content.\n\nDo not redesign. Do not reinterpret. Do not add unnecessary creativity.\n\n**Design fidelity takes precedence over visual novelty.**"
