  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Figma CSS Input**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the Figma CSS output provided. My focus is on understanding the structure and styling to determine the best approach for recreating the landing page. It\'s a complex task, and I\'m looking at all of the elements. I\'m noting the complexity, so I can provide the proper response.\n\n\n**Verifying Page Elements**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the CSS represents the Positivus landing page template from Figma. I\'m focusing on dissecting its sections. Right now, I\'m specifically examining the navigation bar and hero header elements. I see the main components: Logo, navigation links, and a \"Request a quote\" button. Then there is the Heading, Subtext, \"Book a consultation\" button, and illustration. My analysis includes identifying components, and any text replacement rules.\n\n\n**Examining Service Section**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Services\" block. I\'ve identified the section\'s styling, including the green label and heading. I\'ve mapped out the six service cards and the associated text, button, and image elements in the grid layout. I\'m noting the background color variations and specific design elements like the badges and arrows.\n\n\n**Detailing Design Elements**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the elements within the CTA block, noting the card dimensions, background color, and border-radius. I\'m focusing on the text and button styles, and I\'ve also identified the illustration. Next, I am breaking down the structure of the case studies block, focusing on its section heading, background, and the layout of the three-column case study cards. Finally, I\'m examining the structure of the process block, with the accordion cards.\n\n\n**Dissecting Team Composition**\n\nI\'m now focused on the \"Team\" block. I see the green label and heading. Six team member cards arranged in two rows of three are my next task. I am noting the background, border, and shadow styles. Each card contains a masked image, name, role, LinkedIn icon, a divider, and a bio description, along with a \"See all\" button.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Layout**\n\nI\'m now examining the Testimonials and Contact Us blocks. I see the testimonials slider with its cards, each with a quote, author, and navigation. The Contact Us block has a form with radio buttons and input fields. I\'m noting the background colors, border radii, and text styles in each section to understand how they are styled.\n\n\n**Finalizing Element Styles**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the elements within the Footer block. The dark background and rounded corners are first. I am noting the Positivus logo, navigation links, and social icons in the top row. The middle row has contact info and a subscription box. Finally, the copyright information is in the bottom row. I see the green label and button styles. The next step is applying the replacement rules.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Replacement**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the text replacement rules. I will be replacing headings with \"Subtitle,\" and paragraphs with Lorem Ipsum, matching length and line count. I will also be using placeholders for navigation labels and button text like \"Learn More\" to preserve the design. I will focus on visual fidelity and design consistency.\n\n\n"
