  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the visual elements. I\'m taking a close look at the CSS and graphics. I\'ve begun reviewing the images and SVGs referenced in the design. For example, I\'m noting the dimensions of the Positivus Logo in the CSS. Specifically, the width is 219.54px and the height is 36px. I\'ve also noted the \"position\" property being used.\n\n\n**Examining Graphic Details**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the specifics of the Positivus logo and the hero illustration. I\'ve noted the SVG elements of the Positivus icon and how it functions as a 4-point star-flower emblem, distinct from the wordmark. I\'m also analyzing the Hero illustration, specifically its dimensions and the use of rotation. I\'m taking the frame properties of that illustration.\n\n\n**Detailing Service Visuals**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual aspects of the service cards. I\'ve noted the background and badge colors for the SEO card, plus the styling of its link element, including the dark circle, green arrow, and \"Learn more\" text. I\'ve also logged the illustration\'s elements: a magnifier over a search window. The color palette incorporates greens, greys, and a dark tone for the text and link.\n\n\n**Cataloging Service Visuals**\n\nI\'ve just finished documenting the visual characteristics of additional service cards. I\'ve noted the color schemes, link styles (circle and arrow details), and illustration themes for Pay-per-click advertising, Social Media Marketing, Email Marketing, and Content Creation. I\'m focusing on consistency in color and style choices across the different service offerings.\n\n\n**Describing Additional Visuals**\n\nI\'m now describing additional visual elements. I\'ve noted that the analytics and tracking card uses a dark background and green badges with a white link. Its illustration shows volumetric analytics within browser windows. The CTA card features a grey background with rounded corners and a geometric circular illustration. Finally, the case studies section utilizes a dark background with rounded corners, three columns with white dividers, and green \"Learn more\" links.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Interactions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the interactive elements, specifically the \"Learn More\" links with green arrows and the accordion cards. I\'ve noted the default active state of the first accordion card, including its green background, box-shadow, and border radius, along with the font size and weight of the number. The inactive states of the other cards are also logged. I\'m focusing on the toggling functionality, which includes background changes, plus/minus icon switches, and content expansion, creating a smooth visual transition upon user interaction.\n\n\n\n**Describing Team Element Details**\n\nI\'m now describing each team element. I\'m noting the container\'s styles: rounded corners and a dark background with specific padding and shadow. I\'m also logging the avatar\'s custom cutout shape and green blend or mask. I\'m documenting the subtitle, role, and the LinkedIn icon\'s circular styling (black circle, green icon), the divider, and bottom button details.\n\n\n**Defining Interactive Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing the interactive features of the contact section and footer. I\'ve noted the right arrow design, including the interactive carousel navigation, and how clicking left/right switches testimonials, plus updating the active star indicator. I\'m noting that the Contact Us card uses a light background with rounded corners and distinct radio button styling. I\'ve also logged the form fields and dark button details, plus the right side geometric art. Finally, the footer\'s dark background, rounded edges, and layout are cataloged.\n\n\n**Analyzing Footer Structure**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the footer. I\'ve noted the structure: a dark background with rounded corners and a divider line. I see three columns on the left: contact info (logo, address, email, phone) and a copyright notice. On the right, is a subscription box with a rounded, dark background, email input, and a green \"Get Started\" button. I\'m also confirming the text replacement rules, especially those for labels.\n\n\n**Defining Section Headings**\n\nI\'m now detailing section headings. I\'ve confirmed the consistent use of a signature green badge with rounded corners for each title. I\'m noting the CSS for the badge, including font family, size, weight, and color, which confirms it as a key element of the Positivus design system. I\'m also confirming the label structure and button labels with their usage, and defining them to be natural and fitting the width specifications.\n\n\n"
