  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering CSS Adjustments**\n\nI\'m currently considering which CSS utilities and styles to add to `src/index.css`. Specifically, I\'m exploring how to define root styles using Tailwind CSS v4, leveraging either `@theme` or root styles. My focus is now on the `@layer base` directive within the CSS, starting with setting the `font-family` for the `body` element using Space Grotesk.\n\n\n**Defining Base Styles**\n\nI\'ve decided to define root styles. I\'ve begun integrating base styles in CSS for better consistency. I\'ve set up base styles for font properties. Now, I\'m integrating custom utilities for `box-shadow` effects. I am also working on `hover` effects, especially for the `box-shadow` property, to ensure smooth transitions. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and visual fidelity, with emphasis on the shadow effect.\n\n\n**Visualizing UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m visualizing the UI components, focusing on illustration details. I\'m detailing the illustrations for the service cards with distinct concepts. I\'m focusing on the green and black accent colors, including diamond stars. Additionally, I\'m designing a CTA with concentric ellipses. I\'m also planning the process step toggle icon and the testimonials design, including the speech bubbles, stars, and navigation. Furthermore, I\'m considering the contact form and social icons.\n\n\n**Verifying Team Member Photos**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on the team member photos and the CSS needed. I\'m visualizing the unique flower/sprocket masked portraits with a duotone lime green and black/white blend, like Positivus does. I\'ll create high-fidelity SVG portraits for each team member using the exact mask and duotone. Also, I\'m verifying the text replacement rules for headings and paragraphs to ensure layout consistency.\n\n\n**Analyzing Text Replacements**\n\nI am now analyzing text replacement rules. I\'m focusing on how to handle content updates across sections. I\'m inspecting content specifically for the header/hero, main headings, and form placeholders. I\'m using \"Title\" as a stand-in for main headings and updating button labels. I\'m verifying the rules for generic descriptive labels for form placeholders, and now I\'m checking paragraph replacement with Lorem Ipsum. Also, I am considering layout consistency with line count and text density.\n\n\n**Refining Text Replacement**\n\nI\'m now refining text replacement rules, especially for service card headings. I need to maintain line counts. The CSS confirms each service card uses a two-line heading structure (h3 within two labels). I am checking for proper alignment and avoiding layout alterations to make sure they are visually consistent. I need to make sure the replacement text doesn\'t affect the size or position of each element.\n\n\n**Validating Typography Replacements**\n\nI\'m now validating typography replacements across sections to ensure visual consistency and layout integrity. For the service cards, I\'ve confirmed the two-badge heading structure and the two-line heading layout. I\'m checking the Accordion Process, Team cards, testimonials, the CTA, and case studies, to make sure the \"Subtitle\" replacement for headings works as expected and that the Lorem Ipsum placeholder text fits the design constraints.\n\n\n**Reviewing Final Components**\n\nI\'m now reviewing the final components, starting with the contact form and footer. I\'m verifying the \"Say Hi\" and \"Get a Quote\" radio buttons, the name, email, and message fields, and the \"Get Started\" button. The footer navigation labels, the \"Section Title\" badge, contact info, newsletter placeholder and button, and the copyright notice need confirmation too. I\'m also reviewing `Feedback.svg` and `My Website.svg` components and their corresponding CSS comments.\n\n\n**Structuring UI Components**\n\nI\'m now structuring the UI components based on the design blocks. I am organizing code files for each section, including the navbar, hero section with the illustration, and logo strips. I\'ll need to define responsiveness, especially for the logotypes. I\'m planning to make sure Olga\'s attribution is available via a modal or tab, linked to the design references, without cluttering the landing page.\n\n\n**Organizing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now organizing the `src/components` files for the Services, CTA Banner, Case Studies, Working Process, Team, and Testimonials sections. I\'m focusing on implementing their respective components, including badges, subheadings, cards with specific background colors and illustrations, accordions, and buttons. I am also working on adding the necessary styling for layout and interactivity. I\'ll need to define responsiveness across sections.\n\n\n"
