  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Transforming the Logotype**\n\nI\'m currently working on rewriting `src/components/Logotypes.tsx` into a dynamic LED-style marquee. The marquee will display the Vietnamese text: \"Th\341\273\255 th\303\241ch tr\341\273\261c ti\341\272\277p! 2 ng\303\240y Affiliate 100 tri\341\273\207u/ th\303\241ng ch\341\273\211 b\341\272\261ng chi\341\272\277c \304\221i\341\273\207n tho\341\272\241i\" and the background will be a dark LED board style (#191A23) with bright.\n\n\n**Revising Visual Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual style. The aim is a digital ribbon aesthetic, moving away from a static display. I\'m exploring bright lime-green text on a deep-black background, but also experimenting with glow effects, dot markers, and rounded borders. I\'m currently looking at a deep-black background like `#191A23` or `#0D0E12` with lime-green text, resembling a high-tech electronic LED ticker tape.\n\n\n**Refining LED Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve been focusing on refining the LED ticker tape effect. I\'ve integrated a subtle radial gradient overlay to mimic scanlines and added a grid. I\'m also experimenting with a glowing text effect using `drop-shadow` to enhance the visual impact. I\'ve implemented a dot separator and the marquee repeats the text to create a continuous loop with `repeatCount`. I\'m using \"Space Grotesk\" for text. The layout also includes rounded borders.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
