  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **Core Request**: The user wants to update the portrait image in the Hero section (`src/components/Hero.tsx`) with the newly uploaded image `2_585170d0.png` (located at `/public/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png` or `public/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`, referenced in web code as `/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`).\n- **Framing/Cropping Criteria**: \"Cho n\303\263 th\341\272\245y c\303\241i \304\221\341\272\247u v\303\240 n\303\263 m\341\272\245t c\303\241i c\303\271i tr\341\273\217, thay b\341\272\261ng c\303\241i h\303\254nh \341\272\243nh n\303\240y\" (Ensure the top of the head is clearly visible without being clipped, and crop/frame so the elbow/c\303\271i tr\341\273\217 is cut off or bottom-cropped appropriately, rather than clipping the top of the hair/head).\n- **Previous Context**: Rebuilt the Positivus landing page into NAMIND brand with:\n  - Topbar banner in `#B9FF66` above Navbar.\n  - Marquee text replacing sponsors (black text, uppercase, no border lines, no dots).\n  - Hero with title, subtitle, and CTA button opening `RegisterModal.tsx` popup (which has the 3 inputs: T\303\252n, S\304\220T, Email).\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed**:\n  - `src/components/Logotypes.tsx`: Border-y lines removed, running clean black text.\n  - `src/components/RegisterModal.tsx`: Popup window created with 3 textboxes (\"T\303\252n c\341\273\247a b\341\272\241n\", \"S\304\220T c\341\273\247a b\341\272\241n\", \"Email c\341\273\247a b\341\272\241n\"), submit button \"G\341\273\254I V\303\211 MI\341\273\204N PH\303\215 CHO T\303\224I\", and privacy note.\n  - `src/components/Navbar.tsx` and `src/components/Footer.tsx`: Updated to uppercase \"NAMIND\" wordmark without dart/star icon.\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Wired with `RegisterModal`, topbar placed above Navbar without dots.\n- **In Progress / Current Step**:\n  - Updating `src/components/Hero.tsx` with the new image `/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`.\n  - Adjusting container and image positioning (`object-contain` or `object-cover object-top`) so the head/hair is fully visible at the top, while the bottom/elbow (\"c\303\271i tr\341\273\217\") is cropped at the container base.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Image Details\n- `2_585170d0.png` contains the subject with hands crossed/holding wrists, wearing glasses, hoodie, and blazer.\n- In the previous iteration with `1_df3c9a39.png`, using `overflow-hidden` with `scale-[1.46] translate-y-8` cut off the hair/head slightly because the scale pushed the top upward out of the frame.\n- To satisfy \"Cho n\303\263 th\341\272\245y c\303\241i \304\221\341\272\247u v\303\240 n\303\263 m\341\272\245t c\303\241i c\303\271i tr\341\273\217\":\n  - Use `overflow-hidden` at the bottom of the container.\n  - Position image aligned to top: `object-cover object-top` or `object-contain object-top` with `pt-2` or `origin-top` so the head has ample headroom and is never cut off.\n  - The bottom of the frame cuts off the lower elbows / waist cleanly.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Image path: `/public/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png` (browser URL: `/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`).\n- Target file for edits: `src/components/Hero.tsx`.\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Edit `src/components/Hero.tsx`**:\n   - Replace image source from `/assets/aistudio/1_df3c9a39.png` to `/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`.\n   - Update image container styling:\n     ```tsx\n     <div className=\"relative w-full h-[480px] sm:h-[560px] lg:h-[620px] flex items-start justify-center overflow-hidden\">\n       <img\n         src=\"/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png\"\n         alt=\"Ch\303\242n dung \304\221\341\272\241i di\341\273\207n Th\341\273\255 th\303\241ch Affiliate\"\n         className=\"w-full h-full object-cover object-top scale-[1.15] sm:scale-[1.2] origin-top drop-shadow-[0_20px_35px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] select-none pointer-events-none\"\n       />\n     </div>\n     ```\n     *(Adjust scale and `origin-top` so the head is 100% visible with comfortable breathing room at the top, while the bottom/elbows naturally disappear below the overflow edge).*\n2. **Verify Build**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to confirm zero errors.\n3. **Notify User**:\n   - Confirm the new image is set, the head is fully shown, and elbows are neatly cropped at the bottom edge.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must NOT use AI image generation tools; use the exact uploaded PNG `/assets/aistudio/2_585170d0.png`.\n- Do not alter existing texts, popup modal, or NAMIND branding unless requested.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 182
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "D\341\273\261a v\303\240o \304\221\303\242y h\303\243y t\341\272\241o landing page cho t\303\264i\nPrompt nh\306\260 sau\n# PROMPT \342\200\224 RECREATE LANDING PAGE FROM PROVIDED CSS, SVG & IMAGES\n\n## 1. ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n\nAct as a Senior Frontend Developer, UI/UX Designer, and Design System Engineer.\n\nYour task is to build a complete, responsive, production-quality landing page based strictly on the CSS files, SVG assets, images, and other reference materials I provide.\n\n**The primary objective is DESIGN FIDELITY, not creative redesign.**\n\nReconstruct the original visual system as accurately as possible while preserving the existing structure, design language, layout, and graphical assets.\n\n## 2. STRICT DESIGN PRESERVATION\n\nYou MUST preserve the following elements from the provided references:\n\n- Original CSS styling, including colors, gradients, shadows, borders, and effects.\n- Original SVG assets, vector illustrations, shapes, and icons.\n- Original images, including their proportions, crop behavior, and placement.\n- Original typography, including font families, sizes, weights, line heights, and letter spacing.\n- Original spacing system, margins, padding, alignment, and section proportions.\n- Original visual hierarchy and content structure.\n- Original navigation layout, buttons, cards, backgrounds, and section order.\n- Original animations, hover effects, transitions, and visual interactions where provided.\n\n**DO NOT:**\n- Redesign or reinterpret the original interface.\n- Replace supplied SVGs with alternative icons.\n- Generate substitute images when originals are available.\n- Introduce unrelated components or sections.\n- Change the original color palette or design theme.\n- Simplify complex layouts without technical necessity.\n- Apply generic landing page templates.\n- Add decorative elements not present in the references.\n\n## 3. TEXT REPLACEMENT RULES\n\nPreserve the original content structure and placement, but replace the visible textual content with placeholders.\n\nFollow these rules:\n\n**Headings**\n- Replace main headings with \"Title\".\n- Replace section headings with \"Section Title\".\n- Replace smaller headings with \"Subtitle\".\n\n**Paragraphs**\n- Replace paragraph content with Lorem Ipsum.\n- Match the approximate character length and line count of the original text.\n- Preserve the approximate original text density to maintain layout consistency.\n\n**Other text**\n- Navigation labels may use short generic placeholders.\n- Button labels may use \"Learn More\", \"Get Started\", or \"Explore\".\n- Form placeholders may use generic descriptive labels.\n\n**Important:** Do not change the number, order, or visual position of text blocks. Text replacement must not significantly alter the original layout.\n\n## 4. CSS & SVG HANDLING\n\nTreat the provided CSS and SVG files as authoritative design references.\n\n- Reuse original CSS classes and styles whenever technically feasible.\n- Preserve SVG `\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Paste_October_21__2026_-_8_04PM_119bf2ab (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Paste_October_21__2026_-_8_04PM_119bf2ab). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Paste_October_21__2026_-_8_04PM_119bf2ab. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n  User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Style_f04324ed.svg (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Style_f04324ed.svg). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Style_f04324ed.svg. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image gener