I\'m considering whether adding introductory text to subtitles will confuse this straightforward numbering, and the user\'s intent to easily switch content. The user might expect or not expect a bit of extra text in the description, or just \"Subtitle 1\".\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s specific request for numbered titles and subtitles. I see they want direct access, referencing \"Section Title 1\" and \"Subtitle 1\". This is the key. The Figma example used literal quotes for \"Section Title\", and the description for the subtitle. I\'ll make sure each pair is easily accessed, in order, for easy swap-outs. The focus is on literally rendering those texts.\n\n\n**Clarifying Text Examples**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the appropriate examples based on user intentions, considering different scenarios. If the user mentions \"subtitle c\305\251ng th\341\272\277 nha\" after providing a title numbering sequence, I will interpret this literally. The user wants the structure to be direct and predictable. So, \"Section Title 1\" would be paired with \"Subtitle 1,\" unless the user provides an example for subtitle. This structure is designed for straightforward content replacement.\n\n\n"
