  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Subtitle Placement**\n\nOkay, I\'ve identified subtitle use in both `CtaBanner.tsx` and `WorkingProcess.tsx`. I noticed `<h3 ...>Subtitle</h3>` and the `ProcessStep` array with `title: \'Subtitle\'`. This gives me a solid starting point for examining consistent subtitle implementation.\n\n\n**Discovering Design Intent**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I just realized the \"Subtitle\" placeholders are consistent with the original Figma design, where the designer *literally* used \"Subtitle\" as a placeholder across multiple components! The user\'s request for numbered subtitles makes perfect sense now. I\'m moving on to examining the avatar framing request.\n\n\n**Aligning Image and Title**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `Hero.tsx` layout and found the key to aligning the image\'s top with the title\'s top on desktop. Changing `items-center` to `lg:items-start` in the flex container perfectly achieves this alignment. The image will be cropped from the navel up to match the height of the title.\n\n\n"
