  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Input**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s input, particularly the request to reorder and rename a section title, incorporating specific keywords like \"TH\341\273\254 TH\303\201CH 2 NG\303\200Y AFFILIATE T\341\273\260 \304\220\341\273\230NG D\303\222NG TI\341\273\200N 100 TRI\341\273\206U\" and the phrase \"D\303\200NH CHO B\341\272\240N, N\341\272\276U...\". My focus is now on ensuring proper formatting and interpreting the implied meaning. I\'m examining how to handle the \"black box\" content and incorporate the AI reference, and am also considering how this instruction fits into the larger picture.\n\n\n**Clarifying Business Model**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the user\'s frustration with traditional employment and unsuccessful online ventures. The core need seems to be a practical, accessible path to consistent income, emphasizing minimal technical skill and ease of implementation. I\'m focusing on crafting a compelling proposition for an alternative business model, specifically emphasizing the \"black box\" content and mobile-focused approach and need to confirm where the section should be in App.tsx. I am considering ways to clearly articulate the contrast between the proposed solution and the user\'s past experiences with sales and advertising, and how to represent this in the UI.\n\n\n**Reordering Content Sections**\n\nI\'ve successfully reordered the sections as requested, shifting `<CaseStudies />` above `<Services />`. This involved analyzing the specific instruction to move \"Section Title 2\" (mapped to `<CaseStudies />`) before \"Section Title 1\" (mapped to `<Services />`). I\'ve reviewed the `CaseStudies.tsx` content, including its title and badge, to confirm the appropriate section placement.\n\n\n**Interpreting User Intent**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implications of the user\'s request regarding the section title and description. It looks like the section title change is fairly direct. However, I\'m now exploring if the user also wants to modify the description or subtitle associated with it. I\'m carefully re-reading the input to clarify whether a new description is desired, if they want to keep it as is, or if they want it removed. I am checking the current component, but I\'m trying to ensure the user\'s implicit intent, if any, is respected!\n\n\n**Defining User Frustrations**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the core pain points: the user\'s disillusionment with traditional employment and failed online marketing attempts. The goal is to articulate this frustration effectively. I am seeking to highlight a desire for an alternative path. The focus must remain on a practical, phone-based system to generate leads and income, avoiding overly complex technical aspects. The \"black box\" is critical, as is ensuring the tick mark is included.\n\n\n**Refining Display Logic**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal display for the section title and description based on the user\'s input. The long title \"TH\341\273\254 TH\303\201CH 2 NG\303\200Y AFFILIATE T\341\273\260 \304\220\341\273\230NG D\303\222NG TI\341\273\200N 100 TRI\341\273\206U \342\200\223 D\303\200NH CHO B\341\272\240N, N\341\272\276U...\" presents a challenge in terms of visual presentation. However, I\'m noting the potential to omit the description entirely, given the clean look this achieves, especially with the prominent green badge title. I\'m exploring whether the UI framework fully supports this `description=\"\"` scenario and checking the code!\n\n\n**Designing Black Container**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the black container\'s visual presentation, specifically incorporating the four provided items and the requested tick marks. I will ensure the tick marks are at the start of each line within the container. I am keeping in mind the user\'s intent to highlight the contrast and the benefits of the proposed solution within this section. Now I\'m ensuring there is a tick at the start of each of the items I am listing. I am working to ensure they\'re bullet pointed, not numbered.\n\n\n**Visualizing Component Layout**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the design for the black container, deciding between a 2x2 grid or stacked cards for the desktop layout, both of which will revert to a single column on mobile. Within each card, I\'m integrating a bright green checkmark icon in a circle, using the provided SVG. The text within these cards will leverage the specified `Space_Grotesk` font and sizes. I\'m prioritizing readability and visual appeal. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and ensuring the checkmark is properly aligned and sized, to emphasize the key criteria or pain points.\n\n\n**Optimizing Card Layouts**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual presentation of the black container, I will use a dark card design. I\'ve designed a layout with a bright green checkmark, using the provided SVG, and ensured the text is in the specified font and sizes. To ensure optimal readability and visual appeal, I\'m considering a single-column or two-column layout for the cards, testing for different screen sizes. I am focusing on responsiveness and visual balance.\n\n\n**Developing Card Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s pain points into a two-column grid card layout with the previously designed card style, each with a checkmark icon. I\'m focusing on \"kh\303\264ng \304\221\341\272\277n, ti\341\273\201n kh\303\264ng v\341\273\201\", \"m\341\273\207t m\341\273\217i v\341\273\233i m\303\264 h\303\254nh c\305\251,\" and \"mu\341\273\221n m\341\273\231t l\341\273\221i \304\221i kh\303\241c\". The goal is to visually communicate the problems with the \"black box\" model, highlighting the user\'s desire for an easier path to income. I am considering responsiveness across all screen sizes.\n\n\n**Adding CTA Element**\n\nI\'m now integrating a Call-To-Action (CTA) button at the base of the black container, allowing users to register or take immediate action. I am also checking if the user already used this CTA and would like to use a different one! This will use the \"\304\220\304\203ng k\303\275 tham gia ngay\" (Register Now) verbiage. I\'m exploring an `onCtaClick` prop to make this interactive. I am also planning on adding an existing Learn More link as well. I\'m checking existing code to determine appropriate placement.\n\n\n**Refining Call-to-Action**\n\nI\'ve carefully integrated a Call-To-Action (CTA) element within the black container. I\'ve opted for a visually distinct button and incorporated the provided \"Gi\341\273\257 Ch\341\273\227 Ngay B\303\242y Gi\341\273\235\" (Reserve Your Spot Now) verbiage, rather than \"\304\220\304\203ng k\303\275 tham gia ngay\". Now, I\'m ensuring it aligns with the user\'s focus on limited spots, reflecting the initial instruction \"Ch\341\273\211 7 ch\341\273\227 duy nh\341\272\245t\". I am double-checking the code to confirm the button\'s placement and functionality.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating Title Rendering**\n\nI\'m now assessing the `SectionHeading` component\'s ability to handle the lengthy title, particularly the impact of the `shrink-0` class on the green badge container and the responsiveness of the font sizes. I\'m focusing on ensuring it renders correctly on different screen sizes and adjusts appropriately for the long input.\n\n\n**Adjusting Component Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the render issues of the very long title within `SectionHeading`, specifically the impact of `shrink-0` on smaller screens. I am focusing on resolving potential horizontal overflow from `TH\341\273\254 TH\303\201CH 2 NG\303\200Y AFFILIATE T\341\273\260 \304\220\341\273\230NG D\303\222NG TI\341\273\200N 100 TRI\341\273\206U \342\200\223 D\303\200NH CHO B\341\272\240N, N\341\272\276U...` and determining if the badge should wrap or if text adjustments are needed, now that I have reviewed the component\'s code. I\'m taking a moment to reference previous requests.\n\n\n**Refining Title Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing adjustments to the `SectionHeading` component to address the potential for title overflow on smaller screens. Replacing `shrink-0` with `max-w-full inline-block sm:inline-flex` will ensure the long title wraps and remains fully visible across all devices. I\'m focusing on preserving the desktop appearance while maintaining responsive behavior.\n\n\n**Confirming Item Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s provided content into the section items. These include \"B\341\272\241n nh\303\254n AI c\303\240n qu\303\251t, th\341\272\245y r\303\265 c\303\264ng vi\341\273\207c l\303\240m thu\303\252 kh\303\264ng th\341\273\203 \304\221\306\260a b\341\272\241n l\303\252n 100 tri\341\273\207u/th\303\241ng\", \"B\341\272\241n \304\221\303\243 th\341\273\255 b\303\241n h\303\240ng online, \304\221\341\273\225 ti\341\273\201n qu\341\272\243ng c\303\241o\342\200\246 nh\306\260ng kh\303\241ch kh\303\264ng \304\221\341\272\277n, ti\341\273\201n kh\303\264ng v\341\273\201\", and \"B\341\272\241n m\341\273\207t m\341\273\217i v\341\273\233i m\303\264 h\303\254nh c\303\264ng vi\341\273\207c c\305\251: c\303\240ng l\303\240m c\303\240ng k\341\272\271t, thu nh\341\272\255p kh\303\264ng bao gi\341\273\235 v\306\260\341\273\243t ng\306\260\341\273\241ng.\" I\'m reviewing their phrasing and formatting to incorporate them into the visual layout, ensuring a clear presentation.\n\n\n**Integrating User Feedback**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final pain point: \"B\341\272\241n mu\341\273\221n m\341\273\231t l\341\273\221i \304\221i kh\303\241c - th\341\273\261c t\341\272\277, d\341\273\205 l\303\240m - n\306\241i ch\341\273\211 c\341\272\247n bi\341\272\277t b\341\272\245m \304\221i\341\273\207n tho\341\272\241i, b\341\272\241n c\303\263 ngay h\341\273\207 th\341\273\221ng ra kh\303\241ch, ra ti\341\273\201n m\341\272\267t....\" I\'m formatting it for the black container with a tick at the start. I am re-checking the provided `CaseStudies.tsx` code, to ensure each pain point is styled correctly, with bullet points, and the updated content. I am now incorporating this final piece into the UI.\n\n\n**Finalizing Container Styling**\n\nI\'m now incorporating final styling elements for the black container\'s dark card design, focusing on achieving the desired visual hierarchy and balance. I\'ve integrated all of the user\'s provided content into the designed grid layout, ensuring each pain point is presented as its own card. I am finalizing the responsiveness across various screen sizes to ensure a clean, accessible presentation. The integration of all elements is complete!\n\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Presentation**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the black container, ensuring that each of the four cards displays flawlessly on different screen sizes. I\'ve thoroughly reviewed the spacing and alignment of the checkmark icons, text, and overall card layout, making sure the UI conveys the desired contrast and emphasizes the user\'s key pain points. I\'m satisfied with the final result!\n\n\n**Finalizing Code Implementation**\n\nI\'ve now incorporated the final code elements, specifically the dynamic CTA integration for both \"Learn More\" and \"Gi\341\273\257 Ch\341\273\227 Ngay B\303\242y Gi\341\273\235\" buttons. I\'ve confirmed their correct placement and responsiveness. I have also verified the successful move of `<CaseStudies />` to be directly above `<Services />` in `App.tsx`! I\'ve confirmed the layout and overall functionality.\n\n\n"
