  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Component Files**\n\nI\'ve been examining `SectionHeading.tsx` and have isolated the \"Signature Positivus Green Highlight Badge\" section. My focus is on understanding how this visual element is implemented with its specific styling: inline flex, padding, background color, and rounded corners. I\'m noting the use of inline styles versus potentially external CSS classes.\n\n\n**Refining Bold Text Solution**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to best implement the bold text request within the `SectionHeading` component. I\'ve reviewed the existing `SectionHeadingProps` and noticed the potential of using `titleClassName`. Adding this prop to the interface will allow me to pass a custom class name, like \"font-bold,\" directly to the `h2` element. This looks like the most straightforward and flexible solution, which I think is a good approach.\n\n\n**Evaluating Button Implementation**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to the button text and arrow implementation.  I\'m exploring options for the arrow, considering various Unicode characters (like `\360\237\221\211`, `\342\236\224`, or `\342\236\234`) and SVG icons. Currently leaning towards `\360\237\221\211` for a Vietnamese marketing feel, but also evaluating a clean right-arrow SVG. The uppercase text for the button, I\'ve confirmed, will be `NH\341\272\244N V\303\200O \304\220\303\202Y \304\220\341\273\202 GI\341\273\256 CH\341\273\226 NGAY B\303\202Y GI\341\273\234`.\n\n\n"
