  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Call to Action**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the call to action within this visual. The Vietnamese text translates to a limited-time offer, urging immediate reservation by providing information. The right-hand button presumably facilitates this action. I am now considering the best path to action.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the UI elements based on the provided input. I\'ve boldly highlighted the main title text to capture attention and am considering an uppercase button for better visibility. I\'ve also added an arrow icon to the button, to suggest an interactive element and provide strong visual flow from the copy to the call to action. I think this gives a more compelling user interface!\n\n\n**Incorporating Arrow Icons**\n\nI\'m now integrating arrow icons, specifically SVG and Unicode characters like \"\342\206\222\" or \"\360\237\221\211\", before the uppercase Vietnamese text on the button. I\'m keen on exploring both options. I think it will visually reinforce the forward direction of the call to action for a compelling button design. I will use the Vietnamese phrasing \"m\305\251i t\303\252n \304\221\341\272\261ng tr\306\260\341\273\233c\" to guide placement of the icon!\n\n\n**Clarifying Icon Placement**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the placement of the arrow icon. I initially considered it pointing towards the button, but now I understand that \"m\305\251i t\303\252n \304\221\341\272\261ng tr\306\260\341\273\233c\" signifies the icon should be *inside* the button, preceding the text \"NH\341\272\244N V\303\200O \304\220\303\202Y \304\220\341\273\202 GI\341\273\256 CH\341\273\226 NGAY B\303\202Y GI\341\273\234\". It seems standard to add it right before the button text.\n\n\n\n**Enhancing the Title Element**\n\nI\'m now focusing on enhancing the title element. I\'ve noted a specific example with a green accent and bold styling which is more visually striking. I plan to incorporate this style, with a badge, into the `SectionHeading.tsx` component. I\'m prioritizing the visual impact to draw the user\'s attention.\n\n\n**Implementing Title Styling**\n\nI\'m now incorporating styling for the title within the `SectionHeading.tsx` component. I\'ve noted the example with the green highlight and bold font. I\'ve added a `titleClassName` prop, so the section title can be modified. I\'m prioritizing the inclusion of a green badge for the title.\n\n\n"
