    thinking: "**Discovering Component Placement**\n\nI\'ve located \"Subtitle 13\" within the `CtaBanner` component. My focus now shifts to `src/App.tsx`, where I\'m examining the component arrangement. Specifically, I\'m analyzing how the `Hero` component, along with a function `openRegisterModal`, are integrated within the `main` section.\n\n\n**Reordering Component Hierarchy**\n\nI\'ve determined that `CtaBanner` needs to be placed above the `<Services />` component. The target content for that `CtaBanner` should be the \"Subtitle 13\" content, as specified. Furthermore, I will be leaving the `Logotypes` section blank for now. Finally, I will be moving `<CtaBanner onCtaClick={openRegisterModal} />` above the `<Services />` element.\n\n\n**Analyzing Content Sequence**\n\nI\'m now diving into the sequence of content within the `CaseStudies` section, focusing on \"Section Title 2.\" I am reviewing how the supporting text is structured, along with the call to action, specifically the button and its associated text and link, \"Tham gia th\341\273\255 th\303\241ch 2 Ng\303\240y Affiliate >>.\" I\'m carefully observing the flow and structure of the components and supporting text.\n\n\n**Connecting Content Points**\n\nI\'ve established a direct link between the four points describing pain points and \"Subtitle 13.\" This is crucial for the `CaseStudies` section. My plan is to update the `CtaBanner` with new content and button from the image `/public/assets/aistudio/image_9f37dc01.png`. I\'m also confirming the proper placement of all sections in the main section: Hero, Logotypes, CaseStudies, CtaBanner, Services, and WorkingProcess. Now I\'m shifting to inspecting the image for text and design elements, starting with the two heading lines.\n\n\n**Crafting Call to Action**\n\nI\'m now focusing on crafting the content for the updated `CtaBanner`. I\'ve extracted the key text elements: the bold headline, the italicized quote, the call to action with the pointing hand emoji, and the urgent closing statement. I will make a separate blank logo area with vertical spacing, ready for the placeholder image.\n\n\n**Designing Button Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focused on the button design for the `CtaBanner`. I\'ve determined that a large, green button is optimal. I\'m exploring specific hex codes for the green background, aiming for a deep emerald green that matches the provided image. I will implement a rounded corner style, and also configure the white text within, which includes a bold, large font for the main call to action and a normal/medium font for the secondary text. I will ensure it opens the registration modal when clicked and is full width. Furthermore, I will create a blank logo area with vertical spacing.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Layout**\n\nI\'m now examining the container for the `CtaBanner` and comparing it to the image. I see a clean, centered layout with off-white background and centered text. I need to make some adjustments to the original code to make it match. My focus is now on replicating the card-like structure from the image, ensuring all text elements are correctly centered. I will also incorporate a blank logo space.\n\n\n\n**Refining Banner Design**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal background style for the `CtaBanner`. Initial options involved Positivus-style containers or light surfaces, but after re-examining the image, it\'s clear the background should be pure white (`#FFFFFF`). I\'m debating whether to keep the container or set the banner as a distinct section on the page. I\'m referencing the existing `CtaBanner` code, focusing on the background and padding.\n\n\n**Evaluating Container Structure**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the container styling for the `CtaBanner`. I\'m exploring three distinct options: a rounded, light gray container, a container with a light gray background and border, or a pure white background with a border. After reviewing the image, I\'m leaning toward a white background to maintain consistency with the image provided, which confirms a dedicated area for the content of \"\303\224 Subtitle 13\" and the provided image\'s content. I\'m focusing on the \"\303\224 Subtitle 13\" card.\n\n\n\n**Determining Button Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve determined that a white button text against a deep emerald green background within a rounded, off-white card looks best, based on contrast. The exact colors are dark green `#0D7A49` or `#0F7E49` or `#107C41`, with the text and arrows centered with `Space Grotesk`. The top line of the button says \"Tham gia th\341\273\255 th\303\241ch 2 Ng\303\240y Affiliate \302\273\", and the bottom line says \"Nh\341\272\245n v\303\240o \304\221\303\242y \304\221\341\273\203 \304\221\306\260\341\273\243c gi\341\273\257 ch\341\273\227 ngay b\303\242y gi\341\273\235.\" I\'m extracting text and checking a hand icon.\n\n\n**Finalizing CtaBanner Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final text elements into the `CtaBanner`. The title will be: \"N\341\272\277u b\341\272\241n th\341\272\245y m\303\254nh trong b\341\272\245t k\341\273\263 d\303\262ng n\303\240o \341\273\237 tr\303\252n... Th\303\254 TH\341\273\254 TH\303\201CH 2 NG\303\200Y n\303\240y sinh ra ch\303\255nh x\303\241c cho b\341\272\241n!\". Below, I\'ll place the italicized quote: \"V\303\240 b\341\272\241n s\341\272\275 t\341\273\261 h\341\273\217i: \'T\341\272\241i sao \304\221\341\272\277n gi\341\273\235 n\303\240y m\303\254nh m\341\273\233i bi\341\272\277t \304\221\341\272\277n Affiliate\'\". I\'m finalizing the blank space and the new text for the button, adding the 3 arrows (`vvv`), ensuring the overall visual hierarchy aligns with the image and provided text. I will leave the logo section blank.\n\n\n**Confirming Button Behavior**\n\nI\'ve verified that the button click action within the `CtaBanner` correctly triggers the `RegisterModal` via `onCtaClick`, as intended. Additionally, I\'ve checked the component arrangement in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve confirmed that the user\'s request for \"\303\224 Subtitle 13\" corresponds to the `CtaBanner`, which is in the correct section, and that the order is correct.\n\n\n**Positioning Section Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the final text elements into the `CtaBanner`. I\'ve repositioned the `CtaBanner` above `<Services />` and immediately below `<CaseStudies />`. The logical flow is clear: the `CaseStudies` section presents four criteria, immediately followed by the `CtaBanner` which addresses those points. The banner\'s content is finalized, and button functionality is confirmed. I am now leaving the logo section blank.\n\n\n**Refining Text Placement**\n\nI\'m now implementing the complete content for the `CtaBanner` within the `<section>` element. I\'m focusing on text styling, specifically adjusting the bold, italic, and normal text variants. The goal is to accurately represent the provided text elements, including the urgent call to action. I am verifying the appropriate use of spacing and font sizes for a cohesive visual layout, ensuring text alignment and visual hierarchy are maintained, so the banner looks great.\n\n\n**Adjusting Font Sizes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the complete content, centering text, with the goal of visual consistency. My focus is on adjusting the font sizes within the `CtaBanner` to optimize readability and visual hierarchy. I\'m carefully comparing the font sizing, text, and structure for a cohesive visual layout, ensuring text alignment. The banner looks great!\n\n\n**Implementing Final Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided image elements, button, and text formatting to ensure the final layout for the `CtaBanner` is perfect. I\'ve re-examined the design image to verify the button callout, making the text match exactly. I\'ve also focused on spacing, alignment, and sizing of the components, working to ensure the `CtaBanner` section is visually compelling and effectively conveys the intended message.\n\n\n**Finalizing Placement Style**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the final design and placement of the `CtaBanner`. All elements are in place, with correct styling, sizing, and content. The text is readable, the button is compelling, and the overall visual hierarchy is optimized. I\'m focusing on responsiveness across devices, ensuring the banner adapts well to different screen sizes. All elements and sections are now placed correctly.\n\n\n**Evaluating Background Choices**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective background style for the `CtaBanner`. I\'m evaluating options: white, light grey (`#F3F3F3`), and a white background with a border. After reviewing the provided image and other website cards, a light grey background with a border and shadow, similar to other cards (`#F3F3F3` with a border) seems optimal for the distinctive \"\303\224 Subtitle 13\" look, but a white one looks clean, too.\n\n\n**Refining Card Appearance**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the final appearance of the `CtaBanner` card. I\'ve re-evaluated background options, and confirmed a light gray with a border and shadow (`#F3F3F3`) matches other cards. I\'m focusing on text, button style, and overall visual balance. I\'m confident in the structure, text styling, button color choice, and font for the button, to match the image, and am nearly ready to call it complete.\n\n\n"
