    thinking: "**Analyzing User Instructions**\n\nI\'m focusing intently on the user\'s instructions regarding the design elements. I need to understand the specifics: \"C\303\241i n\303\240y \304\221\341\273\203 tr\303\252n \304\221\341\272\247u\" seems to mean \"this goes on top,\" and then the user wants me to avoid excessive highlighting by removing the light green background. I will preserve the highlighted words, only bolding them, according to their request.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Author Placement**\n\nI\'ve decided to prioritize the author information. I\'m placing the author\'s details, including the tagline \"T\341\273\253 m\341\273\231t sinh vi\303\252n b\341\272\255n r\341\273\231n...\", at the very top. This includes the avatar and author\'s name directly above the text, either within the dark card or the letter card itself, removing the need for a bottom-pointing speech bubble tail. The letter starts with this author header.\n\n\n**Refining Author Details**\n\nI\'m now refining the author display. I\'ve placed the provided image, name (\"Nam Anh\"), and tagline (\"T\341\273\253 m\341\273\231t sinh vi\303\252n b\341\272\255n r\341\273\231n...\") at the top. I\'m ensuring it\'s clearly visible within the card design. The light green background highlighting is removed, keeping only the bolded text. I\'ve also removed the light green box background around specific phrases as requested, such as \"Gi\341\272\243i ph\303\241p? Affiliate-T\341\273\261 \304\220\341\273\231ng...\" as well as the 2026 warning!\n\n\n**Highlighting Specific Text**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the text highlighting. I need to ensure the key phrases are visually distinct using the specified color, #B9FF66, and bold formatting. I\'ve identified the elements to highlight and am applying the changes. I\'ve reviewed the text and am making sure the correct words stand out, and the formatting is consistent.\n\n\n**Implementing Text Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing text enhancements. I\'ve focused on clean typography, avoiding background boxes, and bolding key phrases with the specified color, #B9FF66. I\'ve updated the styles, ensuring bold and colored text for \"Gi\341\272\243i ph\303\241p? Affiliate-T\341\273\261 \304\220\341\273\231ng\" and \"N\341\272\277u b\341\272\241n c\303\262n \304\221\341\273\215c \304\221\341\272\277n \304\221\303\242y, b\341\272\241n v\341\272\253n c\303\262n c\341\273\255a \304\221\341\273\203 \304\221\341\273\225i \304\221\341\273\235i.\" I\'m confident that the key sentences are now visually distinct. Also, I\'m examining the container to optimize visual clarity.\n\n\n**Refining Container Design**\n\nI\'m now refining the container\'s appearance, focusing on its visual appeal and structure. I\'m prioritizing the visual hierarchy. I\'m focusing on ensuring a consistent and appealing look by using the specified colors and rounded corners. I am evaluating the use of shadow and border effects. The design of the card utilizes a dark background with a border, and am working to improve its visual clarity and readability.\n\n\n**Focusing on Textual Improvements**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on textual improvements and refinements, specifically highlighting the phrase \"\304\221\341\272\277n ki\341\272\277m \304\221\306\260\341\273\243c th\303\252m h\303\240ng tr\304\203m tri\341\273\207u nh\341\273\235 Affiliate\" to maintain consistency with the provided instructions. I am ensuring that the text is visually clear and readable, applying bolding and the specified color where appropriate. I want to convey the message with emphasis.\n\n\n**Evaluating Text Elements**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the newly provided text elements, paying particular attention to their integration with the existing design and formatting. I\'ll make sure to assess the font, colors, and overall visual hierarchy for a cohesive aesthetic. The aim is to seamlessly blend these new elements within the existing content while maintaining readability and emphasis.\n\n\n**Evaluating Text and Structure**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the new text block and checking for SectionHeading. I\'ve analyzed \"Gi\341\272\243i ph\303\241p? Affiliate-T\341\273\261 \304\220\341\273\231ng\" and the subsequent paragraph. I\'m reviewing the font sizes, colors, and bold formatting to confirm they match the intended style. I also looked at the existing SectionHeading and how it interacts with the newly inserted author information. I\'m making sure everything integrates seamlessly.\n\n\n**Optimizing Header Integration**\n\nI\'m now determining the best approach for the header. If the `SectionHeading` includes `title=\"Tin nh\341\272\257n t\341\273\253 Nam Anh\"`, should I use `description=\"\"`? It feels cleaner and avoids redundancy since the author\'s details are right below. The cropped image confirms the user\'s intent to place the author bar at the top, integrating seamlessly with the letter card. I\'ve placed the details correctly.\n\n\n"
