  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Updating the Brand**\n\nI\'ve just focused on updating the `Footer.tsx` file, specifically line 128, to reflect the uppercase `NAMIND` styling from `PositivusLogo`, using `font-bold text-[30px] uppercase`. The brand name will now render correctly in the footer. I\'m now turning my attention to a new section request, which seems to require a white section with image-based content.\n\n\n**Determining Section Placement**\n\nI\'m now carefully considering where to insert the new section within the application\'s structure, specifically within `src/App.tsx`. I\'ve reviewed the existing component sequence: `Hero`, `Logotypes`, `CaseStudies`, `CtaBanner`, `Testimonials`, `Services`, `WorkingProcess`, `Team`, and `ContactSection`. I\'ve decided this new white section with image-based content should be placed after `CtaBanner`. The image content will be pulled in rather than copying the format from an existing section.\n\n\n**Analyzing Section Context**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the content to understand the new section\'s core message. It\'s clearly about a new affiliate model for non-tech individuals, and a 2-day workshop. I\'m weighing whether to place it directly after `Testimonials` to follow Nam Anh\'s introductory letter or before `Services` to set up the problem-solution dynamic. This placement decision will drive the overall flow.\n\n\n**Evaluating Section Flow**\n\nI\'ve decided on the section\'s optimal placement, placing it directly after the `Testimonials` component, right before `Services`, which creates a compelling narrative flow. I\'m focusing now on the design specifications. This new section requires a clean white background, with image content that doesn\'t borrow from existing formats. The key is pulling the *content* and not the format.\n\n\n**Refining Section Content**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on extracting and refining the textual content from `image_0d2f81eb.png`, ensuring no detail is overlooked. My approach is to avoid direct image embedding or amateur layouts, opting instead for elegant structuring with the established design system: Space Grotesk font, Positivus badge highlights, dark neutral, rounded corners, typography hierarchy, crisp spacing, and responsive two columns. I\'ll maintain a blank placeholder on the right side.\n\n\n**Crafting Section Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating the text with my design. I plan to highlight \"M\341\273\231t m\303\264 h\303\254nh Affiliate M\341\273\232I\" with a #B9FF66 badge. The subtitle will be carefully formatted, including the arrow. The left column will feature three paragraphs, emphasizing the hands-on, practical approach and the transformative nature of the program. I\'ll italicize/bold \"v\305\251 kh\303\255 ki\341\272\277m th\303\252m 100 tri\341\273\207u/th\303\241ng\" and bold \"m\303\240 kh\303\264ng c\341\272\247n bi\341\272\277t c\303\264ng ngh\341\273\207.\" The right column will hold the blank image frame.\n\n\n**Constructing Section Component**\n\nI\'m now building the `AffiliateModelSection.tsx` component, including the interface. I\'m focusing on incorporating a CTA button, and considering its label. The design involves 3/4 or 4/5 rounded corners or a subtle blank card, complete with a dashed border for the image placeholder, and the click handler. I will finalize and make it ready to incorporate the user\'s image.\n\n\n**Implementing Content Styling**\n\nI\'m now incorporating specific text styling into the `AffiliateModelSection`. I\'ve added the #B9FF66 badge for the headline. I\'ve focused on ensuring the text flow reflects the original content\'s emphasis, including bolding and italicizing key phrases like \"v\305\251 kh\303\255 ki\341\272\277m th\303\252m 100 tri\341\273\207u/th\303\241ng\" and bolding \"m\303\240 kh\303\264ng c\341\272\247n bi\341\272\277t c\303\264ng ngh\341\273\207.\" I\'ve also incorporated the arrow icon correctly.\n\n\n**Refining Section Text**\n\nI\'m now integrating more of the textual content. I\'ve focused on ensuring the text flow reflects the original content\'s emphasis. I\'m carefully incorporating the paragraph, \"T\303\264i kh\303\264ng l\303\252n b\341\273\245c \304\221\341\273\203 thuy\341\272\277t gi\341\272\243ng, T\303\264i ng\341\273\223i c\341\272\241nh b\341\272\241n \342\200\223 m\341\273\237 \304\221i\341\273\207n tho\341\272\241i, d\341\273\261ng h\341\273\207 th\341\273\221ng, \304\221\341\273\203 b\341\272\241n t\341\273\261 tay l\303\240m \304\221\306\260\341\273\243c,\" to highlight the hands-on aspect of the workshop.\n\n\n**Finalizing Section Copy**\n\nI\'m now incorporating final touches to the section copy. I\'m focusing on the additional paragraphs, including the \"kh\303\264ng ph\341\272\243i kh\303\263a h\341\273\215c v\303\264 th\306\260\341\273\237ng v\303\264 ph\341\272\241t\" line. I\'m emphasizing the transformative nature of the program with key phrases highlighted. The current copy will be displayed correctly in two separate boxes. I\'m ensuring everything flows cohesively within the established design.\n\n\n\n**Integrating CTA Button**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the CTA button within the `AffiliateModelSection`. I\'ve implemented the `onCtaClick` functionality, including the text, and designed the button style: `w-full sm:w-auto bg-[#191A23] hover:bg-[#B9FF66]`, with an arrow icon. I\'m ensuring it\'s responsive and provides a clear call to action, incorporating the hover effects as well.\n\n\n**Refining Section Layout**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual presentation of the affiliate model section, particularly the image placeholder. I\'m focusing on its aspect ratio and responsiveness to ensure a clean, modern look. I\'m still trying to get the blank card look correct, so the look is clear. I\'m adjusting the styling for the placeholder, refining its border and ensuring it complements the text.\n\n\n\n"
